Description:

Event notifications gain opt-in parameters for special-use attributes
(vnd.fastmail.specialUse, vnd.fastmail.oldSpecialUse), the JMAP ids of the
affected emails (vnd.cmu.emailids) and of the mailboxes
(vnd.fastmail.mailboxJMAPId, vnd.fastmail.oldMailboxJMAPId).  Copy, move and
rename events now always carry oldMailboxUniqueId.

mailboxID is now a URI describing the mailbox, as RFC 5423 defines it,
rather than the mailbox's JMAP id or uniqueid.

vnd.cmu.mbtype, vnd.cmu.mailboxACL and vnd.cmu.visibleUsers are now only
included when listed in event_extra_params; previously they were always
included.

Documentation:

The event_extra_params option in imapd.conf(5).

Config changes:

event_extra_params: new values vnd.fastmail.specialUse, vnd.cmu.emailids and
vnd.fastmail.mailboxJMAPId.

Upgrade instructions:

Consumers that read mailboxID as an id should switch to mailboxUniqueId, or
enable vnd.fastmail.mailboxJMAPId for the value mailboxID used to have.
Deployments that rely on vnd.cmu.mbtype, vnd.cmu.mailboxACL or
vnd.cmu.visibleUsers must add them to event_extra_params.

